WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
space.

2
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.170
Space has always fascinated me.

3
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:09.710
When you see how vast it is, how infinite its scales

4
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.800
are, just at the level of galaxies,

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.300
a lot of what worries me or what I think about life,

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.030
what I want and what I don't want,

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:28.920
kind of like stops making sense.

8
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.610
There are things out there so immense,

9
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:36.160
like a black hole, or a supernova,

10
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:42.390
and we are a mind this complex in a body this fragile,

11
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.770
weak and mortal.

12
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:51.320
It's like a contrast on another scale.

13
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.950
Everything that has happened and will happen in human

14
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.530
history so far, has happened on this planet.

15
00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.670
Everything that has happened on this planet,

16
00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.520
which is one of many in the solar system,

17
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.930
which is one of many in the solar system,

18
00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.520
which is one of many systems in the Milky Way,

19
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.520
which is one of many galaxies in the cluster,

20
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:16.670
which is one of many clusters in the supercluster,

21
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.530
and so on and so on.

22
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:23.660
Like the nearest star is four light years away from

23
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.580
here.

24
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:29.220
Scales are so big that you could just say,

25
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.940
wow, and that's it.

26
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow.

27
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:38.590
Right now, someone in the world is happy about something

28
00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:43.760
that happened to them, and someone is maybe sad.

29
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.020
People are being born, and people are dying.

30
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.210
People are building, and people are destroying.

31
00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.830
It's such a crazy contrast, like it feels like a

32
00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.600
simulation.

33
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.590
Each one of us believes we are special,

34
00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:09.520
but I think that we're more like a character who can

35
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.720
have an effect on the world, but not at the scale of the

36
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.130
universe.

37
00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.980
The universe is indifferent to humans,

38
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:26.680
and instead of rejecting that whole and complex feeling,

39
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.310
I learned how to love it and admire it.

40
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:39.620
It's incredible that we are, but we could be,

41
00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:50.110
the universe experiencing itself in all its greatness.

42
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:56.420
That's why I started looking at lots of space photos

43
00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.820
from the James Webb and the Hubble,

44
00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:06.470
and, well, I would spend hours on a single photo without

45
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.340
listening to anything, immersed,

46
00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.510
absorbed by those images.

47
00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.570
You may wonder whether they are real or not,

48
00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.940
or fake, but I think they are real,

49
00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:27.510
and there is nothing more real in this reality than

50
00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.720
those photos.

51
00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.320
And these are my favorites.

52
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.680
I really have no way to rank them.

53
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:43.120
I don't know which one is better than another.

54
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.980
Some photos are at the scale of stars,

55
00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:52.880
and others at the scale of galaxies.

56
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.510
Where you say, I mean, this part of the photo,

57
00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.930
this small part, is a whole galaxy.

58
00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:07.420
With who knows how many solar systems are in there,

59
00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:12.680
and, well, the idea that we, as humans,

60
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.040
haven't even exploded our whole planet,

61
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.540
it's crazy.

62
00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.800
And since I love these images so much,

63
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.460
I wanted to share them here too.

64
00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.240
And since I love these images so much,

65
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:27.440
I wanted to share them here too.
